OL,3,GNEWSAButler who served royalty shares
OL,4,Ahis etiquette tips
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhen he was a boy growing up in
OL,7,FSuffolk, Julius Smith's grandmother
OL,8,Fwould recall her time working as a cook
OL,9,Fin grand houses where butlers would
OL,10,Fensure life ran smoothly for their
OL,11,Fwealthy employers.
OL,13,FInspired by her stories, Smith enrolled
OL,14,Fin butler school aged 21 and over the
OL,15,Fpast 30 years has worked for royal
OL,16,Ffamilies, including Queen Elizabeth II,
OL,17,Fwho he first served at Helmingham Hall
OL,18,Fnear Stowmarket, Suffolk.
OL,23,APub: 29-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
